[{"_1":2,"_3":4},"root",{"_5":120},"en/routes/conteudo-do-cubo.tsx",{"_5":6},"data",{"_7":8,"_9":10,"_11":12,"_13":14,"_15":-7,"_16":17,"_18":19,"_20":21,"_22":23,"_24":25},"tipo","metodo","cubo",{"_11":118,"_13":118,"_27":119},"id","guimond","nome","Guimond","nomeLongo","termo",{"_27":115,"_116":117},"niveis",[47,71],"introducao","<p>A fast 2x2 method that first twists the corners and only then puts each one in place: white and yellow count the same until the end of orientation. It has 4 steps and ends with the same <a href=\"/en/glossary#pbl\" class=\"termo-do-glossario\" title=\"On the 2x2 (Ortega): puts the pieces of both layers in place at once.\">PBL</a> as <a href=\"/en/glossary#ortega\" class=\"termo-do-glossario\" title=\"A 2x2 method: it builds one face, orients the top one (Ortega OLL) and permutes both layers at once (PBL).\">Ortega</a>, so if you know Ortega you already have half of it. To start, there is a version with just 2 algorithms: <a href=\"/en/2x2/guimond/iniciante\">Guimond with 2 algorithms</a>.</p>\n","etapas",[31,32,33,34],"historias",[26],{"_13":14,"_27":28,"_29":30},"endereco","/historia#guimond","resumo","The method is by Gaétan Guimond, a cuber from Montreal, Canada, who says on his website that he created it in 1982.",{"_11":109,"_13":110,"_37":111,"_39":112,"_41":113,"_42":-7},{"_11":80,"_13":81,"_37":82,"_39":83,"_41":84,"_42":85},{"_11":61,"_13":62,"_37":63,"_39":64,"_41":65,"_42":66},{"_11":35,"_13":36,"_37":38,"_39":40,"_41":-7,"_42":43},"pbl","PBL","html","<p>The same <a href=\"/en/glossary#pbl\" class=\"termo-do-glossario\" title=\"On the 2x2 (Ortega): puts the pieces of both layers in place at once.\">PBL</a> as <a href=\"/en/glossary#ortega\" class=\"termo-do-glossario\" title=\"A 2x2 method: it builds one face, orients the top one (Ortega OLL) and permutes both layers at once (PBL).\">Ortega</a>: both faces are done, the corners just need swapping until the sides match.</p>\n","grupos",[44],"pagina","treino","/2x2/treino?grupo=ortega-pbl",{"_11":45,"_13":45,"_46":47,"_48":49,"_50":51,"_52":53,"_27":54},"Ortega PBL","nivel","iniciante","casos",6,"conjunto",false,"ids",[55,56,57,58,59,60],"/2x2/ortega-pbl","2X2-PBL-Adj","2X2-PBL-Opp","2X2-PBL-OppOpp","2X2-PBL-AdjAdj","2X2-PBL-AdjOpp","2X2-PBL-OppAdj","separacao","Separation","<p>Swap corners between the layers until all the white is on the bottom and all the yellow is on top. There are 6 cases, with short algorithms (1 to 5 turns).</p>\n",[68],{"_13":62,"_27":67},"/2x2/treino?grupo=guimond-separacao","/2x2/guimond/separacao",{"_11":69,"_13":70,"_46":71,"_48":49,"_50":51,"_52":72,"_27":73},"Guimond Separação","Guimond Separation","intermediario",[74,75,76,77,78,79],"/2x2/guimond-separacao","2X2-GS-Vizinhos-e-vizinhos","2X2-GS-Um-e-um","2X2-GS-Tres-e-tres","2X2-GS-Diagonal-e-diagonal","2X2-GS-Diagonal-em-cima","2X2-GS-Diagonal-embaixo","orientacao","Orientation","<p>Leave the top and bottom faces with only white and yellow, mixed. Turn <code>D</code> until the twisted bottom corner is at front-right, and see where its white or yellow points (front or right). Then count how many top corners already have white or yellow facing up: there are 16 cases, almost all with 3 or 4 turns. If all 4 bottom corners are already right, use an <a href=\"/en/glossary#ortega\" class=\"termo-do-glossario\" title=\"A 2x2 method: it builds one face, orients the top one (Ortega OLL) and permutes both layers at once (PBL).\">Ortega</a> <a href=\"/en/glossary#oll\" class=\"termo-do-glossario\" title=\"Makes the top face all one color, without caring about the position of the pieces. There are 57 cases; in 2-Look OLL, 10 cases in two parts.\">OLL</a>.</p>\n",[87],{"_13":81,"_27":86},"/2x2/treino?grupo=guimond-orientacao","/2x2/guimond/orientacao",{"_11":88,"_13":89,"_46":71,"_48":90,"_50":51,"_52":91,"_27":92},"Guimond Orientação","Guimond Orientation",16,[93,94,95,96,97,98,99,100,101,102,103,104,105,106,107,108],"/2x2/guimond-orientacao","2X2-GO-Tres-direita","2X2-GO-Tres-frente","2X2-GO-Vizinhos-frente","2X2-GO-Vizinhos-direita","2X2-GO-Diagonal-frente","2X2-GO-Diagonal-direita","2X2-GO-Um-A-direita","2X2-GO-Um-A-frente","2X2-GO-Um-B-direita","2X2-GO-Um-B-frente","2X2-GO-Um-C-direita","2X2-GO-Um-C-frente","2X2-GO-Nenhum-A-direita","2X2-GO-Nenhum-A-frente","2X2-GO-Nenhum-B-frente","2X2-GO-Nenhum-B-direita","tres-quartos","¾ of a face","<p>Three stickers on the bottom, each white or yellow (they can be mixed). It almost always takes one or two turns: plan it during <a href=\"/en/glossary#inspecao\" class=\"termo-do-glossario\" title=\"The 15 seconds to look at the cube before you start solving, without turning the faces.\">inspection</a>.</p>\n",[],{"_13":110,"_27":114},"/2x2/guimond/tres-quartos","/en/glossary#guimond","dica","A 2x2 method: it twists the corners so white and yellow are on top and bottom (mixed), separates the two colors and finishes with Ortega's…","2x2","/2x2/",{"_121":122,"_123":124},"cubos",[127,128,129,130,131,132],"idiomas",[125,126],"pt","en",{"_11":139,"_13":139},{"_11":118,"_13":118},{"_11":138,"_13":138},{"_11":137,"_13":137},{"_11":135,"_13":136},{"_11":133,"_13":134},"pyraminx","Pyraminx","megaminx","Megaminx","5x5","4x4","3x3"]
